<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:controls="clr-namespace:KinesisEdit.Controls"
             xmlns:views="clr-namespace:KinesisEdit.Views"
             xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:KinesisEdit.ViewModels"
             mc:Ignorable="d" d:DesignWidth="244" d:DesignHeight="420"
             x:Class="KinesisEdit.Views.TokenPickerView"
             x:DataType="vm:TokenPickerViewModel">
  <!--
    The token picker (mockups 1e/2a): a query, a live counter, the filter chips and the grouped
    result rows. It is the whole of §11.6's searchable list, drawn once and hosted twice — inline in
    the key inspector's Remap panel, and inside the macro-insertion modal.

    IT CARRIES NO RECORD BUTTON. Mockup 1e draws `● Record` beside the search field; here it sits
    beside the current-assignment field one row up, in Views/RemapPanelView.axaml. Two reasons, both
    stated there: Record arms keystroke capture, which this control knows nothing about and must not
    learn in order to stay reusable in a modal that has no capture at all; and the rail is 268 px
    wide, where a field, a counter and a button on one line leaves the field too narrow to show what
    was typed into it. The pairing is the same one the Tap and Hold panel uses — the field, and the
    button that fills it.

    THE MONO LAW, ROW BY ROW. `[esc]` is mono because layoutN.txt contains exactly that; the action's
    name, the scope, the group headers and the counter are the app talking about the file and are
    sans. That is also why the query box is `searchField` and not `monoValue`: it holds what the user
    is looking for, never a value the file carries.

    TWO MARKS ARE DRAWN RATHER THAN TYPED. The `↵` of the assign hint here, and the `●` of the Record
    button next door. Neither U+21B5 nor U+25CF is in either embedded IBM Plex family (checked
    against the glyph typefaces), so both would fall through to a platform substitute and tofu where
    there is none — the same finding that turned mockup 1e's `⌕` into the Path the SearchField theme
    draws.
  -->
  <StackPanel Spacing="8">

    <!-- ===== The query and the counter =======================================================
         A Grid rather than a horizontal StackPanel: a StackPanel measures its children with
         infinite width, so the field would never shrink to the rail and the counter would be
         pushed off the edge. -->
    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
      <!-- A real TextBox, and the one place in this panel where that is right: capture stands down
           while focus sits in one, so the query is typed rather than swallowed as a keystroke. The
           theme draws the leading `⌕` itself, as a Path. -->
      <TextBox Grid.Column="0"
               Classes="searchField"
               Text="{Binding Query, Mode=TwoWay}"
               Watermark="{x:Static vm:TokenPickerViewModel.SearchLabel}" />

      <!-- Matches over the whole catalog of this dialect. Both numbers are derived — the
           denominator is KeySearchCatalog.Build(dialect).Count — and neither is mono: a count is
           the app counting, not a value any file contains. -->
      <TextBlock Grid.Column="1"
                 Text="{Binding CounterText}"
                 Classes="meta muted"
                 VerticalAlignment="Center" />
    </Grid>

    <!-- ===== The chips =======================================================================
         `All · Letters · Nav · Media · Mouse · Hotkeys · Recent`, on the FilterChip control theme
         that #86 wrote and left without a call site. A WrapPanel, because seven chips never fit one
         268 px line; below TokenPickerViewModel.NarrowWidth the picker hides `Mouse` and `Hotkeys`,
         which is mockup 2a's reduced row — a responsive rule, not a second chip set. -->
    <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Categories}">
      <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
        <ItemsPanelTemplate>
          <WrapPanel />
        </ItemsPanelTemplate>
      </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
      <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
        <DataTemplate DataType="vm:TokenPickerCategoryViewModel">
          <Button Classes="filterChip"
                  Classes.selected="{Binding IsSelected}"
                  IsVisible="{Binding IsShown}"
                  Margin="0,0,4,4"
                  Content="{Binding Caption}"
                  CommandParameter="{Binding}"
                  Command="{Binding $parent[views:TokenPickerView].((vm:TokenPickerViewModel)DataContext).SelectCategoryCommand}" />
        </DataTemplate>
      </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
    </ItemsControl>

    <!-- A query that matches nothing says so, rather than leaving an empty box that reads as a
         broken list. Muted prose, never an error: nothing failed. -->
    <TextBlock Text="{x:Static vm:TokenPickerViewModel.NoMatchesMessage}"
               Classes="body muted"
               TextWrapping="Wrap"
               IsVisible="{Binding !HasMatches}" />

    <!-- ===== The results =====================================================================
         Counted headers with their rows beneath them. The header is outside the row containers on
         purpose: a header drawn inside one would take the selection fill along with the row.

         The rows are ListBoxItems on the SelectableListRow container theme, laid out by an
         ItemsControl rather than selected by a ListBox — the list is grouped, and one ListBox per
         group would be one independent selection per group. `IsSelected` is bound instead, which is
         what raises the theme's own `:selected` face, and the picker keeps exactly one row carrying
         it. -->
    <ScrollViewer Classes="tokenPickerResults" HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
      <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Groups}">
        <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
          <DataTemplate DataType="vm:TokenPickerGroupViewModel">
            <Border Classes="tokenPickerGroup">
              <StackPanel Spacing="2">
                <!-- `Navigation · 3`. Sans, deliberately: `sectionLabel` is the app's usual caption
                     role and it is mono, which the mono law reserves for file values. -->
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Header}"
                           Classes="pill muted"
                           TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                           Margin="0,0,0,2" />

                <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Rows}">
                  <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate DataType="vm:TokenPickerRowViewModel">
                      <ListBoxItem Theme="{StaticResource SelectableListRow}"
                                   IsSelected="{Binding IsSelected}"
                                   Tapped="OnRowTapped"
                                   DoubleTapped="OnRowDoubleTapped">
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="8">
                          <!-- The token as the file spells it. -->
                          <TextBlock Grid.Column="0"
                                     Text="{Binding Token}"
                                     Classes="monoValue"
                                     VerticalAlignment="Center" />

                          <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}"
                                       Classes="meta"
                                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                            <!-- Where the row lives on the board, or — for a duplicate registration
                                 — the row it duplicates, named by that row rather than by its
                                 token: a real alias spells the SAME token as its canonical, so
                                 "alias of [numlk]" would appear on the [numlk] row itself. -->
                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding Detail}"
                                       Classes="meta muted"
                                       IsVisible="{Binding HasDetail}"
                                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                          </StackPanel>

                          <!-- `↵ assign`, on the row ↵ would take. -->
                          <StackPanel Grid.Column="2"
                                      Orientation="Horizontal"
                                      Spacing="4"
                                      VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                      IsVisible="{Binding IsSelected}">
                            <controls:Icon Classes="assignHint"
                                           Data="M 13,3 L 13,9 L 4,9 M 7,6 L 4,9 L 7,12"
                                           VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Static vm:TokenPickerRowViewModel.AssignHint}"
                                       Classes="meta muted"
                                       VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                          </StackPanel>
                        </Grid>
                      </ListBoxItem>
                    </DataTemplate>
                  </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                </ItemsControl>
              </StackPanel>
            </Border>
          </DataTemplate>
        </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
      </ItemsControl>
    </ScrollViewer>
  </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
